WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
I want to begin in Volume 13, and this is May the first 1921.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The human will casts dissimilarity between the creator and the creature.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
For one who lives in the divine will, everything is harmony.

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:26.000
So, Luisa said, "Continue in my usual state, I found myself outside of myself in the

5
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
midst of a multitude of people." And Op High, there was the Queen Mother.

6
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Now, Op High always means living in the divine will, living the great eagle on the

7
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
mountain. And she was speaking to that people, and she was crying so much, in fact,

8
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
that holding a bunch of roses on her lap, she wet them with her tears.

9
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
I could not understand anything of what she was saying.

10
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
I could only see that the people wanted to make two molds, and that the celestial

11
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.000
mother was praying them, crying to calm down.

12
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.000
And then she detached one rose, and pointing to me, in the midst of so many

13
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.000
people, she threw it to me. I looked at it.

14
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.000
The rose was paralleled with the tears of my dear mother, and those tears

15
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.000
invited me to pray for the peace of these peoples.

16
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Now, here we see a lovely image of Mary as the mother of all people.

17
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:39.000
She was constituted mother at the foot of the cross, and here she is interceding

18
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:45.000
for her children, wanting to bring them to peace and to harmony with God.

19
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Then afterwards, I found myself together with my sweet Jesus, and I prayed him

20
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.000
for the peace of the peoples, and he, drawing me to myself, spoke to me about

21
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.000
his most holy will. Now, in the middle of all this intercession, our lady

22
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.000
pointed Louisa out as the one to intercede, because Louisa was the victim

23
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:17.000
soul, and she was also called to open up the kingdom of the divine will.

24
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.000
So naturally, she was the one that was pointed to.

25
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:27.000
So Jesus explains the mission given to Louisa and through her to the rest of us.

26
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:32.000
"My daughter," he said, "my will contains the creative power."

27
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Now, he keeps saying this, and we need to take it on board, that when we enter

28
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.000
into the divine will and make the divine will our own, we have that creative power

29
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:48.000
in our hands. And this creative power is what originated the universe.

30
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.000
It's the source of the three fiats.

31
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.000
"My will," he said, "contains the creative power.

32
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.000
And just as my will gave life to all things."

33
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:04.000
So you have Genesis 1 and 2. You have Colossians 1, 16.

34
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.000
You have Ephesians 1, 10.

35
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.000
It gave life to everything.

36
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Of course, also, you have John chapter 1, verses 1 to 5.

37
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.000
It gave life to all things, so it gave physical life.

38
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:27.000
It gave spiritual life, because the divine will is the source of all life.

39
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Of course, you have John 14, 6 as well.

40
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.000
"I am the way, the truth, and the life."

41
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.000
So, "my will" contains the creative power.

42
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:47.000
And just as my will gave life to all things, so it has the power to destroy them.

43
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:53.000
So for this, I want to give you Jeremiah chapter 1, verses 9 to 10,

44
00:03:53.000 --> 00:04:00.000
where Jeremiah was told that he was called to build up and plant and to build up

45
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.000
and to break down and destroy as well.

46
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Now, the soul who lives in my volition also has the power to give life,

47
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:17.000
life to that which is good, and to give debt to that which is evil,

48
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.000
to plant, to build up, to break down and destroy.

49
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.000
So, I also want to give you Jeremiah chapter 10, verses 6 to 15,

50
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.000
and verses 23 to 24.

51
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.000
So, let's read that again. It's actually very important.

52
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:41.000
The soul who lives in my volition also has the power to give life to good

53
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.000
and to give death to evil.

54
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:49.000
So, the very fact of being in the divine will means that we are very much

55
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:57.000
participators in this spiritual warfare that is going on continuously.

56
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.000
It has just come to mind, the same Paul said,

57
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.000
"The weapons of our warfare are not carnal,

58
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:10.000
but they are mighty in pulling down the strongholds of evil."

59
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.000
And that's what is referred to here, to give death to evil.

60
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:21.000
In the immensity of the divine will, the soul finds herself in the past,

61
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:26.000
and wherever there are voids to my glory, or fences to be repaired,

62
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:31.000
love not given to me, she fills the voids of my glory.

63
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:36.000
She makes for me the most beautiful reparations,

64
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.000
and she gives me love for everybody.

65
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:46.000
In my will, she diffuses herself in the present.

66
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:54.000
She extends to the future centuries, and everywhere, and for everyone,

67
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.000
she gives me that which creation owes me.

68
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:04.000
So, you see that the mission we have is very great and very extensive.

69
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.000
It covers the past, the present, and the future.

70
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:11.000
All souls from Adam to Zachary, A to Z.

71
00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:15.000
In the soul who lives in my will, I hear the echo of my power,

72
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.000
of my love, and of my sanctity.

73
00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:25.000
In all my acts, I hear the echo of hers.

74
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.000
She runs everywhere before me, behind me, and even inside of me.

75
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.000
Wherever my will is, there is hers.

76
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:42.000
As my acts multiply themselves, hers also multiply.

77
00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:48.000
Only the human will puts disharmony between the creator and the creature.

78
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:55.000
One single act of the human will puts chaos between heaven and earth.

79
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.000
Chaos is a big word now,

80
00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:04.000
because it means disharmony disintegration, things falling apart.

81
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:10.000
One single act of the human will puts chaos between heaven and earth,

82
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:17.000
and it casts dissimilarity between the creator and the creature.

83
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:23.000
On the other hand, for one who lives in my will, everything is harmony.

84
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.000
Her things and mine harmonize together.

85
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:33.000
I am with her on earth, and she is with me in heaven.

86
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:40.000
We have the same interest, the same life, and there's only one will between us.

87
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.000
This really doesn't require a comment.

88
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:50.000
It does require a lot of meditation and thinking and praying.

89
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:55.000
To live in the divine will is to have one will and one life.

90
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.000
You're living on earth and you're also living in heaven.

91
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:04.000
And the divine will is living in heaven and also living on earth.

92
00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.000
So I want to give you John 14-21.

93
00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:14.000
You and me and I in you, both completely one.

94
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:20.000
See, because creation has not moved from my will in anything,

95
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.000
because creation wasn't given any free will.

96
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:27.000
So it moves only in the will of God.

97
00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.000
The sky is always Asia blue.

98
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.000
It's always starry.

99
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.000
The sun is always full of light and heat.

100
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.000
The whole of creation is in perfect harmony.

101
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:45.000
One thing is the support of the other.

102
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.000
There's no individual will in battle against any other will.

103
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.000
So everything is in harmony.

104
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.000
Everything supports one another.

105
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.000
So it's always beautiful.

106
00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:02.000
It's always fresh and it's always young.

107
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.000
It never grows old.

108
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.000
Nor does it lose one shadow of its beauty.

109
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:18.000
On the contrary, it seems that each day the divine will rises as more majestic,

110
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:23.000
giving a sweet enchantment to all creatures.

111
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:29.000
So would man have been if he had not withdrawn from my will?

112
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:35.000
And so are the souls who actually do live in my will.

113
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:39.000
So let me look at what he has just said.

114
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.000
So are the souls who live in my will.

115
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.000
They are always beautiful, always fresh, always young.

116
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.000
They never grow old.

117
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.000
They don't lose their beauty.

118
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:55.000
On the contrary, each day the divine will grows more beautiful in them.

119
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.000
It's wonderful.

120
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.000
They are the new heavens, the new suns and the new earth,

121
00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:05.000
the all flowery, even more varied with beauty and enchantment.

122
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:14.000
This is the new Jerusalem which you will find described in John 21, sorry, not John.

123
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:24.000
This is the new Jerusalem described in the book of Revelation, chapter 21 and 22.

124
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:28.000
So may the 21st 1921.

125
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:35.000
Jesus finds rest in the souls who live in his will.

126
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:42.000
As I was in my usual state, Louisa said, "My beloved Jesus made himself seen in my arms

127
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.000
in the act of taking rest.

128
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:52.000
I clashed into my heart, saying to him, 'My love, say a word to me, why are you silent?'

129
00:10:52.000 --> 00:11:00.000
It has occurred to me to say a word about what Louisa means by her usual state.

130
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.000
Louisa's usual state is a state of ecstasy.

131
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:13.000
She sits there in the bed, hour upon hour upon hour in communion with God.

132
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:17.000
Sometimes she has an out of the body experience.

133
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.000
Sometimes she doesn't.

134
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:22.000
Visions and revelations are perfectly normal for her.

135
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:27.000
So normal in fact that she complains if she doesn't have it.

136
00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.000
So now she wants a revelation.

137
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:37.000
That's the meaning of a word, a davar in Hebrew.

138
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:42.000
On Mount Sinai, God gave ten words to the people,

139
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:51.000
which we unfortunately call ten commandments as if he was thundering from on high.

140
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:59.000
He gave ten words, ten revelations to show us how weak and broken, and in that case

141
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:06.000
unredeemed human beings could actually live together in harmony.

142
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:13.000
So Jesus continues, 'My beloved daughter, rest is necessary to me.

143
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:20.000
And having spoken to you so much, I want in you the first effects of my words.

144
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:26.000
So you must work doing what I have taught you, and I will rest.'

145
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:30.000
This is the pattern you find in the Bible.

146
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:36.000
In Genesis chapter 1, God did the work of creation, and then he rested.

147
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:42.000
In the gospel of Saint John, you have Jesus doing the work of redemption,

148
00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:48.000
and then he rests on the Sabbath day before the resurrection.

149
00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:55.000
And I deliberately say John's gospel because John brings it out much more than the other three gospels do.

150
00:12:55.000 --> 00:13:04.000
And so what Jesus is saying is that in us, when he reveals something to us in the divine will,

151
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:08.000
he's doing the work of revealing.

152
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:15.000
But then we must do the work of putting it into practice.

153
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:22.000
And as we put it into practice, that gives him rest, and then he will go to work again.

154
00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:30.000
But of course, before he actually gives us the revelation, he has to work in us to dispose us, to receive it.

155
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:38.000
He has to prepare our souls so that we're actually able to accept the revelation.

156
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:53.000
Very often he has to expand our soul in order that there is enough space in us for this new revelation that he's going to make.

157
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.000
So let me repeat that again.

158
00:13:55.000 --> 00:14:00.000
My beloved daughter rest is necessary to me.

159
00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:06.000
After having spoken to you so much, I want in you the first effects of my words.

160
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:12.000
So you must work doing what I have taught you and I will rest.

161
00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:18.000
And when you have put my teachings into execution, that means you actually put them into practice.

162
00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:24.000
I will come back again to speak to you of higher and more sublime things.

163
00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:34.000
So we don't deserve the higher and more sublime things if we haven't put the lower things into practice.

164
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:43.000
If you put that in a different way, you don't put the roof on the house until you put the foundations in and you built up the walls.

165
00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:48.000
Otherwise, it would be monumentally stupid.

166
00:14:48.000 --> 00:15:03.000
So I want to give you James, chapter 1, verses 22 to 25, where he says that you must not just listen to the word, you must also put it into practice.

167
00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:13.000
So Jesus will come back and tell us higher and more sublime things if we have put the lower foundational things into practice.

168
00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:22.000
I will come back again, he said, to speak to you of higher and more sublime things, to be able to find rest more beautiful in you.

169
00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:31.000
And besides, if I do not rest in the souls who live in my will, in whom could I hope to rest?

170
00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:38.000
Because if the others are not even listening to him, let alone putting something into practice.

171
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:45.000
Only the souls who live in my will are capable of giving me rest.

172
00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:50.000
Now we're going to see that this rest is union with God.

173
00:15:50.000 --> 00:16:01.000
The living in my will forms the room or the space or the tabernacle for Jesus.

174
00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:08.000
The act on in my will form for me the bed or the resting place.

175
00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:26.000
The repeated acts, the constancy in repeating are the lullabies, so the constancy in repeating our acts are the lullabies, the music and the opium to favor my sleep.

176
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:47.000
Now you'll notice that this is 1921, and at that particular stage, opium had been discovered as something that really can not only put you to sleep, but can actually go much deeper and make a drug addict out of you and cause all kinds of hallucinations and everything.

177
00:16:47.000 --> 00:17:02.000
But at that particular stage, they didn't know the negative side of opium. They didn't realize that opium had to be taken in very small doses if you were to benefit from it.

178
00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:17.000
And so the thing that fascinates me is that whatever has been discovered on earth, Jesus will mention it. He'll mention electricity and all the rest of it.

179
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:35.000
"But while I sleep," he said, "I watch over you in such a way that your will is nothing other than the outpouring of mine. Your thoughts, the outpouring of my intelligence, your word, the outpouring of mine, your heart, the outpouring of mine."

180
00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:59.000
So even though you don't hear me speak, there is such dissolving of yourself in me. That's your John 14, 21, and also Galatians 2, 20, "I no longer live, Christ lives in me."

181
00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:12.000
So even though you don't hear me speak, there is such dissolving of yourself in me that you do not want or think or do anything but what I myself want and do.

182
00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:25.000
So as long as you live in my will, you can be sure that everything that goes on within you is me. There is a description of union with God.

183
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:31.000
And this is the glory of our lives. And this is what we're called to.

184
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:38.000
You go back to the beginning of this, and he said, "He has to dispose us to be able to receive what he's giving us."

185
00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:47.000
So he gives us his revelation and his word. We take it on board. We put it into practice. We start living this.

186
00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:55.000
And as we start living this, he is able to make room for himself. He's able to make a new tabernacle on earth.

187
00:18:55.000 --> 00:19:01.000
So for that room or that tabernacle, I want to give you one Corinthians 3, 16.

188
00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:07.000
And he's able to make this space or this tabernacle for himself.

189
00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:17.000
And then the acts on in his will form the place where he can rest the manger, if you like. He says, "Bed here."

190
00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:29.000
And the repeated act and the constancy in repeating that we don't give up are the lullabies and the music and the opium to favour sleep.

191
00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:37.000
Now notice that Jesus mentions lullabies, music and opium to help sleep.

192
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:52.000
He's talking about people having trouble to sleep. They're not lying down in bed and just knocking over into an absolutely restful sleep.

193
00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:57.000
He's talking about people who need help to get into that sleep mode.

194
00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:04.000
And we know that children love stories and that babies love lullabies.

195
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:14.000
And that infants absolutely love really good music.

196
00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:25.000
I remember watching a child who was only a couple of months old on the floor listening to Mozart and absolutely loving it.

197
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:28.000
They loved the harmony.

198
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:37.000
But if you gave the same child some of the modern music with all its frenetic, hellish beat, the child would cry.

199
00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:42.000
It was the harmony that was touching the harmony that was in the child.

200
00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:50.000
And so in order to favour sleep, we need that peace, we need that harmony.

201
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:57.000
And so he's touching on the fact that we need to come into harmony with him.

202
00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:07.000
And that as we come into harmony with him, it's like him receiving lullabies.

203
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:19.000
And when our will comes into harmony with his, it's like him having that taste of opium that sends him into a very quiet, deep sleep.

204
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:24.000
But he's not sleeping like we do, not at all.

205
00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:34.000
When Jesus was on earth in the incarnation, as he slept at night.

206
00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:38.000
I don't know if he slept the whole night, every night, I doubt it.

207
00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:46.000
But as he slept, he was also God governing the universe,

208
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:50.000
bringing children to birth and taking people in death.

209
00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:54.000
He was also being the sovereign Lord of the universe.

210
00:21:54.000 --> 00:22:03.000
And so he's saying here that while our acts enable him to rest and to sleep in us, at the same time,

211
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:15.000
while this is happening, he said, "While I sleep, I watch over you in such a way that your will is nothing other but the outpouring of mine."

212
00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:23.000
That means that as we surrender to him, we allow his will to operate through us.

213
00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:26.000
This is what is required.

214
00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:32.000
It allows his intelligence to come through our thoughts.

